     1	"""EKF that tracks one rover's planar pose plus body-frame speed.
     2	
     3	State model
     4	-----------
     5	    s = [x, y, theta, v, omega]        (mm, mm, rad, mm/s, rad/s)
     6	
     7	    dx/dt     = v * cos(theta)
     8	    dy/dt     = v * sin(theta)
     9	    dtheta/dt = omega
    10	    dv/dt     = (v_cmd - v) / tau + w_v          (w_v: random-walk accel noise)
    11	    domega/dt = (omega_cmd - omega) / tau + w_om  (w_om: random-walk alpha noise)
    12	
    13	This is the lead's candidate (unicycle + first-order-lag speed states) and it is
    14	kept after evaluating the alternative.
    15	
    16	Why not [x, y, vx, vy, theta, omega] (a free planar rigid body)?
    17	A differential-drive rover cannot slide sideways: the wheel contact constraint pins
    18	the BODY-FRAME lateral velocity to (approximately) zero at all times -- it is not a
    19	quantity that varies and needs its own filter state, it is a constraint. Estimating
    20	world-frame [vx, vy] is, after rotating into the body frame, equivalent to estimating
    21	[v_forward, v_lateral] where v_lateral's true value is always ~0. But nothing in the
    22	process model or in the measurements (vision gives position + heading only, never a
    23	velocity) ties v_lateral back to zero: process noise injects independent uncertainty
    24	into vx and vy every step, so the lateral component is a pure random walk with no
    25	corrective term. Its variance grows unboundedly between vision fixes and, because
    26	theta itself is uncertain, that spurious lateral energy rotates into the x/y estimate
    27	-- an unobservable mode contaminating the very quantity we care about. This is exactly
    28	the "redundant, unobservable-lateral-velocity" problem flagged by the lead. The
    29	unicycle state sidesteps it structurally: v and omega are the ONLY velocity states and
    30	the nonholonomic constraint is baked into the kinematics (dx/dt, dy/dt both scale off
    31	the single scalar v), so there is no lateral-velocity component to mis-estimate.
    32	
    33	Bonus, and the reason this also satisfies the "fuse IMU/odometry later without a
    34	redesign" requirement: v and omega already being explicit states means a gyro
    35	(measures omega directly, H = [0,0,0,0,1]) or wheel odometry (measures v and omega via
    36	wheel speeds, H = [[0,0,0,1,0],[0,0,0,0,1]]) are both simple *linear* observations of
    37	existing states -- addable as new update_* methods with no change to the state vector
    38	or the process model.
    39	
    40	Numerics
    41	--------
    42	predict() and the vision-replay path share one integrator (`_advance`) that walks the
    43	recorded command history and, within each constant-command segment, sub-steps at
    44	`_MAX_SUBSTEP_S` using a midpoint (explicit RK2) integration of the mean plus its
    45	analytic Jacobian for the covariance (`P' = F P F^T + Q`). Process noise (accel_noise,
    46	alpha_noise) is injected on the v/omega diagonal each sub-step and is carried into
    47	x/y/theta by F over subsequent steps -- the standard, widely-used approximation for
    48	random-walk-driven unicycle EKFs (it skips the exact double integral of noise over the
    49	step, which is negligible at the sub-step sizes used here).
    50	
    51	Latency handling: measurements arrive with capture time t_capture <= t_now. A rolling
    52	list of (t, x, P) checkpoints (spanning `cfg.history_s`) lets update_vision rewind to
    53	t_capture, apply the correction there, and replay forward through the recorded command
    54	history to t_now -- rather than smearing a stale correction onto the current state.
    55	
    56	Vision feed quirk (frozen frames): when >= 2 corner markers are occluded, the official
    57	feed keeps publishing (increasing seq) but repeats the SAME t_capture and unchanged
    58	object age. Such a repeat carries no new information and must not reset the "age since
    59	last accepted fix" clock or count as an outlier rejection. `update_vision` therefore
    60	compares t_capture against the last *processed* capture time (not just gates it through
    61	Mahalanobis) and drops exact duplicates / anything out of order before doing any work.
